**What is prohibited.** GitHub does not allow any projects that are designed for, encourage, promote, support, or suggest in any way the use of large language models or any other synthetic or manipulated media tools for creating [1]:

- Sexual material involving minors, or any other content that would constitute Child Sexual Abuse Material under GitHub policies;
- Violent extremist propaganda, or any other content that would constitute Terrorist or Violent Extremist Content under GitHub policies;
- Sexually explicit media of people without their consent, or any other content that would constitute Non-Consensual Intimate Imagery under GitHub policies.

**How violations are assessed.** GitHub evaluates violations of this policy by examining a project *in context*. Factors that may be considered include how a project is configured; how it is marketed; the information provided in its README or other documentation; the external sites or resources it links to; the nature of support provided by the project maintainers; or any other relevant facts indicating a likelihood of furthering one of the prohibited uses above [1]. GitHub retains full discretion to act on violations, including account suspension, termination, or content removal [2].

